            <div xml:id="d1552">

                <pb facs="1300" n="1196" xml:id="pg1196"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 723.2515/134.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1910-04-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 12, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have learned from the British Minister that he and the French Chargé d’Affaires
                    have received instructions to offer their moral support to the Argentine
                    Republic in settling Chile-Peru dispute; and that he had telegraphed said
                    instructions to the British Legations at Santiago and Rio de Janeiro. He asked
                    if I had similar instructions. I replied by referring him to the Department of
                    State, Washington.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sherrill</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
